+- id: head-identity-gate-pre-push-identity
+  subsystem: ci
+  lifecycle: active
+  files: ["scripts/head-identity-gate.mjs", "hooks/pre-push", "src/run-task.ts", "test/**", "plan/tasks.d/**"]
+  fact: >-
+    Before the first push of a branch, give its head an identity the head-identity gate accepts: a
+    run-shaped ref (`run-<taskId>-<epochMs>` for a filed task, `run-unfiled-<epochMs>` for unfiled
+    work), or an anchored `Remudero-Task: <id>` trailer on the head commit. A branch shaped
+    codex/ or claude/ is refused at push, and the gate names the rename, which only works while the
+    branch is still free. Once a pull request is open its head ref cannot be renamed, so the repair
+    is a new head commit carrying the trailer (`git commit --allow-empty`), never an amend or a new PR.
+  evidence: >-
+    The head-identity gate refused pull requests #10671 and #10760 in one window, and each was
+    repaired after the refusal. The gate's refusal text (scripts/head-identity-gate.mjs) names both
+    run-branch forms and the trailer route, and it refuses at push before a pull request exists. The
+    root cause of each refusal was not read from the PR diffs or the gate's logs, so this entry names
+    the identity step a fix lane must take before pushing, not a verified per-PR cause.
+  src: "ci-learning:10671:head-identity-gate"
+  cited: "2026-10-11"
